module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Chow.TensorZeroScheme.Branches
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Chow.ZeroSchemePullback.LocalEquation
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Divisors.InvertibleSheafSum
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Divisors.ZeroSchemeData
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Divisors.ZeroSchemeFactorization
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.InvertiblePullbackFlat.SectionGenerator
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Properties.PrincipalOpens.Sections

/-!
# The tensor product of two trivializations, and the local equation of a product of sections

Let `X` be a scheme, let `M` and `N` be invertible `𝒪_X`-modules and let `U` be an affine open on
which both are trivial, the triviality being given as `Γ(X, U)`-linear equivalences
`eM : Γ(M, U) ≃ₗ Γ(X, U)` and `eN : Γ(N, U) ≃ₗ Γ(X, U)`. This file tensors the two
trivializations into a trivialization of `M ⊗ N` over `U` under which the local equation of a
pure tensor of sections is the product of their local equations, and reads off the ideal of the
zero scheme of a product of two global sections on such an open:

`Z(a ⊗ b)(U) = (eM (a|_U) · eN (b|_U))`.

That identity is the affine-local content of condition (5) of [Stacks, Tag 0F97]: the two
branches `Z(a)` and `Z(b)` of the zero scheme of `a ⊗ b` are cut out on `U` by the two factors of
the single generator of `Z(a ⊗ b)`.

The last section makes this usable after a base change `g : X' ⟶ X`: a trivialization of `M` over
`U` induces one of `g^*M` over any affine open `U'` of `X'` inside `g⁻¹(U)`, and under it the local
equation of `g^*a` is the image `g.appLE U U' h (e (a|_U))` of the local equation of `a`. So the
displayed identity survives pullback, with each factor replaced by its image.

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.Divisors.generatorSectionsOfLinearEquiv`: the trivializing section determined by a
  trivialization on an affine open, as a
  `Stacks.Cohomology.Generators.GeneratorSections` — i.e. together with the fact that it
  generates over *every* open inside the affine one.
* `Stacks.Divisors.tensorTrivialization`: **the tensor product of two trivializations**, a
  `Γ(X, U)`-linear equivalence `Γ(M ⊗ N, U) ≃ₗ Γ(X, U)`.

## Main results

* `Stacks.Divisors.bijective_smul_symm_one`: a trivialization of an invertible module on an
  affine open generates the sections over every open inside it. This is what upgrades a single
  linear equivalence on `U` to the sheaf-level trivialization the tensor product needs.
* `Stacks.Divisors.tensorTrivialization_tensorSection`: **the local equation of a pure tensor is
  the product of the local equations**, `tensorTrivialization eM eN (m ⊗ n) = eM m · eN n`.
* `Stacks.Divisors.tensorTrivialization_map_tensorSection`: the same for the restriction to `U` of
  a pure tensor of two *global* sections.
* `Stacks.Divisors.zeroScheme_ideal_tensorSection`: **the ideal of `Z(a ⊗ b)` on `U` is generated
  by `eM (a|_U) · eN (b|_U)`**. This is the form the consumer uses.
* `Stacks.Divisors.exists_linearEquiv_pullbackSection` and
  `Stacks.Divisors.exists_linearEquiv_pullbackGlobalSections`: **a trivialization pulls back**, and
  the local equation of a pulled-back section is the image of its local equation.
* `Stacks.Divisors.zeroScheme_ideal_pullbackGlobalSections`: the ideal of `Z(g^*a)` on `U'` is
  generated by `g.appLE U U' h (e (a|_U))`.

## Implementation notes

*Why the hypothesis is only a linear equivalence on `U`, and what has to be proved.* The existing
tensor-of-trivializations result,
`Stacks.Cohomology.Generators.bijective_smul_toTensorSheafSection`, consumes a
`Stacks.Cohomology.Generators.GeneratorSections` — a section generating over every smaller open,
which is sheaf-level data. A single `Γ(M, U) ≃ₗ Γ(X, U)` is weaker on its face. On an *affine*
open it is not: the sections of a quasi-coherent module over a basic open of an affine open are
the localization of the sections over that open
(`AlgebraicGeometry.isLocalizedModule_restriction_basicOpen_of_qcqs`), so the preimage `m₀` of `1`
still generates there; comparing it with a local generator supplied by
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.exists_bijective_smul_of_isInvertible` exhibits the comparison factor as a
unit, and generation then spreads to every open inside `U` because it is local
(`Stacks.SheafOfModules.bijective_smul_of_forall_exists_bijective_smul`). That chain is
`Stacks.Divisors.bijective_smul_symm_one`, and it is the only real work in the file; everything
after it is bilinearity of `Stacks.Divisors.tensorSection` and
`Stacks.Divisors.zeroScheme_ideal_of_trivialization`.

*The two spellings of the tensor product.* `Stacks.Divisors.tensorModules` is
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.TensorSheafification.tensorSheaf`, while
`Stacks.Cohomology.Generators.bijective_smul_toTensorSheafSection` is stated at
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.TensorStalkRingedSpace.tensorSheaf`. The two are the same term
(`Stacks.TensorSheafDedup.tensorSheaf_eq` is `rfl`), as are `Stacks.Divisors.tensorSection` and
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.TensorStalkRingedSpace.toTensorSheafSection` on a pure tensor, so no
transport is needed and none is written.

*Bilinearity is taken from the linear maps, not re-proved.* `Stacks.Divisors.tensorSectionRight`
and `tensorSectionLeft` are already `LinearMap`s, so writing a section as its coordinate times the
trivializing section and pulling the coordinate out is `map_smul` twice.

*The pullback half runs through the base-change comparison, and is written in term mode.* On a pair
of affine opens the comparison `AlgebraicGeometry.affinePullbackSectionsBaseChangeIso` identifies
`Γ(g^*M, U')` with `Γ(X', U') ⊗_{Γ(X, U)} Γ(M, U)`, carrying `1 ⊗ b` to the pullback of `b`; the
trivialization transports the second factor to `Γ(X, U)`, so the pullback of the trivializing
section generates and the pullback of `b` is `g.appLE (e b)` times it. As in
`AlgebraicGeometry.pullbackSection_eq_zero_iff_of_iso` the comparison is kept as a *parameter* in
`Stacks.Divisors.exists_linearEquiv_pullbackSection_of_iso`: the two spellings of `1 ⊗ b` — through
the `Module` instance of the notation and through the one the extension of scalars is taken along —
are definitionally but not syntactically equal, so the comparison applied to a pure tensor is not
type-correct at `implicit` transparency and no `rw` may touch it. Every step of that proof is
therefore a `congrArg`/`Eq.trans` chain, and the two tensor computations it needs are the
standalone algebraic lemmas `Stacks.Divisors.bijective_tmul_symm_one` and
`Stacks.Divisors.tmul_one_eq_tmul_symm_one`, applied with their `Module` instance given
explicitly.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0F97](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0F97)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 02OQ](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/02OQ)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01P7](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01P7)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0B8M](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0B8M)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0B6Y](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0B6Y)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open AlgebraicGeometry CategoryTheory TopologicalSpace Opposite
open Stacks.Cohomology.Generators (GeneratorSections)
open scoped ChangeOfRings TensorProduct

universe u

namespace Stacks.Divisors

variable {X : Scheme.{u}}

/-! ### Algebraic preliminaries -/

/-- Multiplication by a unit of a commutative ring is bijective. -/
theorem bijective_mul_right_of_isUnit {R : Type*} [CommRing R] {c : R} (hc : IsUnit c) :
    Function.Bijective (fun r : R => r * c) := by
  obtain ⟨u, rfl⟩ := hc
  refine ⟨fun r r' h => ?_, fun s => ⟨s * (↑u⁻¹ : R), ?_⟩⟩
  · have h' := congrArg (fun z : R => z * (↑u⁻¹ : R)) h
    simpa [mul_assoc] using h'
  · simp [mul_assoc]

/-- A unit multiple of a basis of a free rank-one module is again a basis. -/
theorem bijective_smul_unit_smul {R M : Type*} [CommRing R] [AddCommGroup M] [Module R M]
    {c : R} (hc : IsUnit c) (p : M) (hp : Function.Bijective (fun r : R => r • p)) :
    Function.Bijective (fun r : R => r • (c • p)) := by
  have hfun : (fun r : R => r • (c • p)) = (fun r : R => r • p) ∘ (fun r : R => r * c) :=
    funext fun r => (mul_smul r c p).symm
  rw [hfun]
  exact hp.comp (bijective_mul_right_of_isUnit hc)

/-- Under a linear equivalence `M ≃ₗ[R] R`, a linear map out of `M` is determined by its value on
the preimage of `1`. -/
private theorem apply_eq_smul_symm_one {R M P : Type*} [CommRing R] [AddCommGroup M]
    [Module R M] [AddCommGroup P] [Module R P] (f : M →ₗ[R] P) (e : M ≃ₗ[R] R) (m : M) :
    f m = e m • f (e.symm 1) :=
  calc f m = f (e.symm (e m • (1 : R))) := by rw [smul_eq_mul, mul_one, e.symm_apply_apply]
    _ = e m • f (e.symm 1) := by rw [map_smul, map_smul]

/-- Under a linear equivalence `M ≃ₗ[R] R`, every element of `M` is its own coordinate times
the preimage of `1`. -/
theorem eq_smul_symm_one {R M : Type*} [CommRing R] [AddCommGroup M] [Module R M]
    (e : M ≃ₗ[R] R) (m : M) : m = e m • e.symm 1 :=
  apply_eq_smul_symm_one LinearMap.id e m

/-! ### Restriction bookkeeping -/

/-- Restricting a section twice is restricting it once. -/
theorem map_map_of_le (L : X.Modules) {A B C : X.Opens} (hBA : B ≤ A) (hCB : C ≤ B)
    (hCA : C ≤ A) (t : Γ(L, A)) :
    L.presheaf.map (homOfLE hCB).op (L.presheaf.map (homOfLE hBA).op t) =
      L.presheaf.map (homOfLE hCA).op t := by
  rw [← ConcreteCategory.comp_apply, ← Functor.map_comp]
  congr 2

/-! ### A trivialization on an affine open generates on every smaller open -/

/-- **A trivialization of an invertible module over an affine open generates the sections over
every basic open inside it.** The sections over a basic open are the localization of the sections
over the affine open, so the preimage of `1` under the trivialization, which generates the latter,
generates the former. -/
theorem exists_smul_eq_of_isAffineOpen (L : X.Modules) [L.IsQuasicoherent]
    {U : X.Opens} (hU : IsAffineOpen U) (e : Γ(L, U) ≃ₗ[Γ(X, U)] Γ(X, U)) (g : Γ(X, U))
    (y : Γ(L, X.basicOpen g)) :
    ∃ a : Γ(X, X.basicOpen g),
      a • L.presheaf.map (homOfLE (X.basicOpen_le g)).op (e.symm 1) = y := by
  let : Module Γ(X, U) Γ(L, X.basicOpen g) :=
    Module.compHom Γ(L, X.basicOpen g)
      (X.presheaf.map (homOfLE (X.basicOpen_le g)).op).hom
  have hloc : IsLocalizedModule.Away g
      (Scheme.Modules.restrictionLinearMap L (homOfLE (X.basicOpen_le g))) :=
    isLocalizedModule_restriction_basicOpen_of_qcqs L hU.isCompact hU.isQuasiSeparated g
  obtain ⟨⟨m, s⟩, hms⟩ := IsLocalizedModule.surj (Submonoid.powers g)
    (Scheme.Modules.restrictionLinearMap L (homOfLE (X.basicOpen_le g))) y
  have hms' : X.presheaf.map (homOfLE (X.basicOpen_le g)).op (s : Γ(X, U)) • y =
      L.presheaf.map (homOfLE (X.basicOpen_le g)).op m := hms
  obtain ⟨n, hn⟩ := s.2
  have hu : IsUnit (X.presheaf.map (homOfLE (X.basicOpen_le g)).op (s : Γ(X, U))) := by
    rw [← hn, map_pow]
    exact (X.toRingedSpace.isUnit_res_basicOpen g).pow n
  obtain ⟨u, hu'⟩ := hu
  have hm : L.presheaf.map (homOfLE (X.basicOpen_le g)).op m =
      X.presheaf.map (homOfLE (X.basicOpen_le g)).op (e m) •
        L.presheaf.map (homOfLE (X.basicOpen_le g)).op (e.symm 1) :=
    (congrArg (L.presheaf.map (homOfLE (X.basicOpen_le g)).op) (eq_smul_symm_one e m)).trans
      (Scheme.Modules.map_smul L (homOfLE (X.basicOpen_le g)) (e m) (e.symm 1))
  refine ⟨(↑u⁻¹ : Γ(X, X.basicOpen g)) *
    X.presheaf.map (homOfLE (X.basicOpen_le g)).op (e m), ?_⟩
  rw [mul_smul, ← hm, ← hms', ← hu', ← mul_smul, u.inv_mul, one_smul]

/-- **A trivialization on an affine open generates on a neighbourhood of each of its points, and
on every open inside that neighbourhood.** The neighbourhood is a basic open of the affine open
small enough that the module is trivial on it in the strong sense of
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.exists_bijective_smul_of_isInvertible`; there the preimage of `1` under the
trivialization and the local generator differ by a factor which divides and is divided by `1`,
hence is a unit. -/
theorem exists_nhd_bijective_smul_symm_one (L : X.Modules)
    [AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsInvertible X.sheaf.obj X.ringCatSheaf.property L]
    {U : X.Opens} (hU : IsAffineOpen U) (e : Γ(L, U) ≃ₗ[Γ(X, U)] Γ(X, U)) {x : X} (hx : x ∈ U) :
    ∃ (W : X.Opens) (_ : x ∈ W) (hWU : W ≤ U),
      ∀ (K : X.Opens) (hK : K ≤ W),
        Function.Bijective
          (fun r : Γ(X, K) => r • L.presheaf.map (homOfLE (hK.trans hWU)).op (e.symm 1)) := by
  have : L.IsQuasicoherent := isQuasicoherent_of_isInvertible L
  have : Stacks.SheafOfModules.IsInvertible X.presheaf
      (structureSheafRing X.toRingedSpace).property L :=
    (Stacks.SheafOfModules.isInvertible_iff_algebraicGeometry X.presheaf
      (structureSheafRing X.toRingedSpace).property L).2 ‹_›
  obtain ⟨W₀, hxW₀, a, ha⟩ :=
    Stacks.SheafOfModules.exists_bijective_smul_of_isInvertible (X := X.toRingedSpace) L x
  obtain ⟨g, hgle, hxg⟩ := hU.exists_basicOpen_le (V := U ⊓ W₀) ⟨x, ⟨hx, hxW₀⟩⟩ hx
  have hBW : X.basicOpen g ≤ W₀ := hgle.trans inf_le_right
  have hp : ∀ (K : X.Opens) (hK : K ≤ X.basicOpen g),
      Function.Bijective (fun r : Γ(X, K) =>
        r • L.presheaf.map (homOfLE (hK.trans hBW)).op (a : Γ(L, W₀))) :=
    fun K hK => ha K (hK.trans hBW)
  obtain ⟨c, hc0⟩ := (hp (X.basicOpen g) le_rfl).surjective
    (L.presheaf.map (homOfLE (X.basicOpen_le g)).op (e.symm 1))
  have hc : c • L.presheaf.map (homOfLE hBW).op (a : Γ(L, W₀)) =
      L.presheaf.map (homOfLE (X.basicOpen_le g)).op (e.symm 1) := hc0
  obtain ⟨d, hd⟩ := exists_smul_eq_of_isAffineOpen L hU e g
    (L.presheaf.map (homOfLE hBW).op (a : Γ(L, W₀)))
  have hcu : IsUnit c := by
    have key : (d * c) • L.presheaf.map (homOfLE hBW).op a =
        (1 : Γ(X, X.basicOpen g)) • L.presheaf.map (homOfLE hBW).op a := by
      rw [mul_smul, hc, hd, one_smul]
    have hdc : d * c = 1 := (hp (X.basicOpen g) le_rfl).injective key
    exact IsUnit.of_mul_eq_one d (by rw [mul_comm]; exact hdc)
  refine ⟨X.basicOpen g, hxg, X.basicOpen_le g, fun K hK => ?_⟩
  have h1 : L.presheaf.map (homOfLE hK).op
        (L.presheaf.map (homOfLE (X.basicOpen_le g)).op (e.symm 1)) =
      L.presheaf.map (homOfLE (hK.trans (X.basicOpen_le g))).op (e.symm 1) :=
    map_map_of_le L _ _ _ _
  have h2 : L.presheaf.map (homOfLE hK).op (c • L.presheaf.map (homOfLE hBW).op a) =
      X.presheaf.map (homOfLE hK).op c • L.presheaf.map (homOfLE (hK.trans hBW)).op a := by
    rw [Scheme.Modules.map_smul]
    exact congrArg _ (map_map_of_le L hBW hK (hK.trans hBW) a)
  have hres : L.presheaf.map (homOfLE (hK.trans (X.basicOpen_le g))).op (e.symm 1) =
      X.presheaf.map (homOfLE hK).op c • L.presheaf.map (homOfLE (hK.trans hBW)).op a := by
    rw [← h1, ← hc]
    exact h2
  rw [hres]
  exact bijective_smul_unit_smul
    (IsUnit.map (X.presheaf.map (homOfLE hK).op).hom hcu) _ (hp K hK)

/-- **A trivialization of an invertible module over an affine open generates the sections over
every open inside it.** Generation is local on the open
(`Stacks.SheafOfModules.bijective_smul_of_forall_exists_bijective_smul`) and
`Stacks.Divisors.exists_nhd_bijective_smul_symm_one` supplies it locally. -/
theorem bijective_smul_symm_one (L : X.Modules)
    [AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsInvertible X.sheaf.obj X.ringCatSheaf.property L]
    {U : X.Opens} (hU : IsAffineOpen U) (e : Γ(L, U) ≃ₗ[Γ(X, U)] Γ(X, U))
    (V : X.Opens) (hV : V ≤ U) :
    Function.Bijective
      (fun r : Γ(X, V) => r • L.presheaf.map (homOfLE hV).op (e.symm 1)) := by
  refine Stacks.SheafOfModules.bijective_smul_of_forall_exists_bijective_smul
    (X := X.toRingedSpace) (L := L)
    (L.presheaf.map (homOfLE hV).op (e.symm 1)) fun y hy => ?_
  obtain ⟨W, hyW, hWU, hbij⟩ := exists_nhd_bijective_smul_symm_one L hU e (hV hy)
  refine ⟨W ⊓ V, ⟨hyW, hy⟩, inf_le_right, fun K hK => ?_⟩
  have h : Function.Bijective (fun r : Γ(X, K) =>
      r • L.presheaf.map (homOfLE (hK.trans (inf_le_right : W ⊓ V ≤ V))).op
        (L.presheaf.map (homOfLE hV).op (e.symm 1))) := by
    rw [map_map_of_le L hV (hK.trans (inf_le_right : W ⊓ V ≤ V))
      ((hK.trans (inf_le_left : W ⊓ V ≤ W)).trans hWU) (e.symm 1)]
    exact hbij K (hK.trans inf_le_left)
  exact h

/-- **The trivializing section determined by a trivialization on an affine open**, as a
`Stacks.Cohomology.Generators.GeneratorSections`: the preimage of `1`, which generates the
sections over every open inside the affine one. -/
def generatorSectionsOfLinearEquiv (L : X.Modules)
    [AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsInvertible X.sheaf.obj X.ringCatSheaf.property L]
    {U : X.Opens} (hU : IsAffineOpen U) (e : Γ(L, U) ≃ₗ[Γ(X, U)] Γ(X, U)) :
    GeneratorSections X.toRingedSpace L U :=
  ⟨e.symm 1, fun V hV => bijective_smul_symm_one L hU e V hV⟩

/-! ### The tensor product of two trivializations -/

variable (M N : X.Modules)
  [AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsInvertible X.sheaf.obj X.ringCatSheaf.property M]
  [AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsInvertible X.sheaf.obj X.ringCatSheaf.property N]

/-- **The pure tensor of two trivializing sections trivializes the tensor product.** -/
theorem bijective_smul_tensorSection {U : X.Opens} (hU : IsAffineOpen U)
    (eM : Γ(M, U) ≃ₗ[Γ(X, U)] Γ(X, U)) (eN : Γ(N, U) ≃ₗ[Γ(X, U)] Γ(X, U)) :
    Function.Bijective (fun r : Γ(X, U) =>
      r • tensorSection M N U (eM.symm 1) (eN.symm 1)) :=
  Stacks.Cohomology.Generators.bijective_smul_toTensorSheafSection X.toRingedSpace M N U
    (generatorSectionsOfLinearEquiv M hU eM) (generatorSectionsOfLinearEquiv N hU eN)

/-- **The tensor product of two trivializations.** On an affine open trivializing both `M` and
`N`, the pure tensor of the two trivializing sections trivializes `M ⊗ N`, and the resulting
trivialization sends a pure tensor of sections to the product of their local equations
(`Stacks.Divisors.tensorTrivialization_tensorSection`). -/
def tensorTrivialization {U : X.Opens} (hU : IsAffineOpen U)
    (eM : Γ(M, U) ≃ₗ[Γ(X, U)] Γ(X, U)) (eN : Γ(N, U) ≃ₗ[Γ(X, U)] Γ(X, U)) :
    Γ(tensorModules M N, U) ≃ₗ[Γ(X, U)] Γ(X, U) :=
  (LinearEquiv.ofBijective
    (LinearMap.toSpanSingleton Γ(X, U) Γ(tensorModules M N, U)
      (tensorSection M N U (eM.symm 1) (eN.symm 1)))
    (bijective_smul_tensorSection M N hU eM eN)).symm

/-- The inverse of the tensor product of two trivializations is multiplication by the pure
tensor of the two trivializing sections. -/
theorem tensorTrivialization_symm_apply {U : X.Opens} (hU : IsAffineOpen U)
    (eM : Γ(M, U) ≃ₗ[Γ(X, U)] Γ(X, U)) (eN : Γ(N, U) ≃ₗ[Γ(X, U)] Γ(X, U)) (r : Γ(X, U)) :
    (tensorTrivialization M N hU eM eN).symm r =
      r • tensorSection M N U (eM.symm 1) (eN.symm 1) := rfl

omit [AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsInvertible X.sheaf.obj X.ringCatSheaf.property M]
  [AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsInvertible X.sheaf.obj X.ringCatSheaf.property N] in
/-- The section of `M ⊗ N` cut out by a pair of sections is the product of their coordinates
times the pure tensor of the two trivializing sections. -/
theorem tensorSection_eq_smul {U : X.Opens}
    (eM : Γ(M, U) ≃ₗ[Γ(X, U)] Γ(X, U)) (eN : Γ(N, U) ≃ₗ[Γ(X, U)] Γ(X, U))
    (m : Γ(M, U)) (n : Γ(N, U)) :
    tensorSection M N U m n =
      (eM m * eN n) • tensorSection M N U (eM.symm 1) (eN.symm 1) := by
  have h1 : tensorSection M N U m n = eM m • tensorSection M N U (eM.symm 1) n := by
    rw [← tensorSectionRight_apply, apply_eq_smul_symm_one (tensorSectionRight M N U n) eM m,
      tensorSectionRight_apply]
  have h2 : tensorSection M N U (eM.symm 1) n =
      eN n • tensorSection M N U (eM.symm 1) (eN.symm 1) := by
    rw [← tensorSectionLeft_apply,
      apply_eq_smul_symm_one (tensorSectionLeft M N U (eM.symm 1)) eN n, tensorSectionLeft_apply]
  rw [h1, h2, smul_smul]

/-- **The local equation of a pure tensor of sections is the product of their local equations.**
-/
theorem tensorTrivialization_tensorSection {U : X.Opens} (hU : IsAffineOpen U)
    (eM : Γ(M, U) ≃ₗ[Γ(X, U)] Γ(X, U)) (eN : Γ(N, U) ≃ₗ[Γ(X, U)] Γ(X, U))
    (m : Γ(M, U)) (n : Γ(N, U)) :
    tensorTrivialization M N hU eM eN (tensorSection M N U m n) = eM m * eN n := by
  refine (LinearEquiv.eq_symm_apply _).mp ?_
  rw [tensorTrivialization_symm_apply]
  exact tensorSection_eq_smul M N eM eN m n

/-! ### The local equation of the zero scheme of a product of global sections -/

/-- **The local equation of a product of two global sections is the product of their local
equations.** -/
theorem tensorTrivialization_map_tensorSection (U : X.affineOpens)
    (eM : Γ(M, U.1) ≃ₗ[Γ(X, U.1)] Γ(X, U.1)) (eN : Γ(N, U.1) ≃ₗ[Γ(X, U.1)] Γ(X, U.1))
    (a : Γ(M, ⊤)) (b : Γ(N, ⊤)) :
    tensorTrivialization M N U.2 eM eN
        ((tensorModules M N).presheaf.map (homOfLE le_top).op (tensorSection M N ⊤ a b)) =
      eM (M.presheaf.map (homOfLE le_top).op a) *
        eN (N.presheaf.map (homOfLE le_top).op b) := by
  rw [tensorSection_restrict M N (homOfLE (le_top : U.1 ≤ ⊤)) a b]
  exact tensorTrivialization_tensorSection M N U.2 eM eN _ _

/-- **The ideal of the zero scheme of `a ⊗ b` on a trivializing affine open** is generated by the
product of the local equations of `a` and of `b`. -/
theorem zeroScheme_ideal_tensorSection (U : X.affineOpens)
    (eM : Γ(M, U.1) ≃ₗ[Γ(X, U.1)] Γ(X, U.1)) (eN : Γ(N, U.1) ≃ₗ[Γ(X, U.1)] Γ(X, U.1))
    (a : Γ(M, ⊤)) (b : Γ(N, ⊤)) :
    (zeroScheme X (tensorModules M N) (tensorSection M N ⊤ a b)).ideal U =
      Ideal.span ({eM (M.presheaf.map (homOfLE le_top).op a) *
        eN (N.presheaf.map (homOfLE le_top).op b)} : Set Γ(X, U.1)) :=
  zeroScheme_ideal_of_trivialization X (tensorModules M N) (tensorSection M N ⊤ a b) U
    (tensorTrivialization M N U.2 eM eN) _
    (tensorTrivialization_map_tensorSection M N U eM eN a b)

/-! ### Compatibility with pullback -/

/-- **A base change of a free rank-one module is free of rank one on the preimage of its basis.**
Under a trivialization `e : N ≃ₗ[R] R`, the map `t ↦ t ⊗ e.symm 1` is a bijection `S → S ⊗[R] N`:
its inverse is the composite of `e` on the second factor with the right unitor. -/
theorem bijective_tmul_symm_one {R S N : Type*} [CommRing R] [CommRing S] [Module R S]
    [AddCommGroup N] [Module R N] (e : N ≃ₗ[R] R) :
    Function.Bijective (fun t : S => t ⊗ₜ[R] e.symm 1) := by
  set Θ : S ⊗[R] N ≃ₗ[R] S :=
    (TensorProduct.congr (LinearEquiv.refl R S) e).trans (TensorProduct.rid R S) with hΘ
  have hΘt : ∀ t : S, Θ (t ⊗ₜ[R] e.symm 1) = t := by
    intro t
    rw [hΘ]
    simp
  have hfun : (fun t : S => t ⊗ₜ[R] e.symm 1) = Θ.symm :=
    funext fun t => (Θ.symm_apply_eq.mpr (hΘt t).symm).symm
  rw [hfun]
  exact Θ.symm.bijective

/-- In a base change along `φ`, the pure tensor `1 ⊗ b` is the local equation of `b` tensored
with the basis `e.symm 1`. -/
theorem tmul_one_eq_tmul_symm_one {R S N : Type*} [CommRing R] [CommRing S] [Module R S]
    [AddCommGroup N] [Module R N] (φ : R →+* S) (hsmul : ∀ (r : R) (t : S), r • t = φ r * t)
    (e : N ≃ₗ[R] R) (b : N) :
    (1 : S) ⊗ₜ[R] b = φ (e b) ⊗ₜ[R] e.symm 1 :=
  calc (1 : S) ⊗ₜ[R] b = (1 : S) ⊗ₜ[R] (e b • e.symm 1) := congrArg _ (eq_smul_symm_one e b)
    _ = (e b • (1 : S)) ⊗ₜ[R] e.symm 1 := (TensorProduct.smul_tmul _ _ _).symm
    _ = φ (e b) ⊗ₜ[R] e.symm 1 := by rw [hsmul, mul_one]

/-- **A trivialization pulls back, with the base-change comparison as a parameter.** The
comparison is kept opaque for the reason recorded in
`AlgebraicGeometry.pullbackSection_eq_zero_iff_of_iso`: the two spellings of `1 ⊗ b` — through the
`Module` instance induced by `g.appLE` and through the ring map the extension of scalars is taken
along — are definitionally equal, and under a named comparison checking that unfolds the
comparison. -/
theorem exists_linearEquiv_pullbackSection_of_iso {X' : Scheme.{u}} (g : X' ⟶ X)
    (M : X.Modules) {U : X.Opens} {U' : X'.Opens} (hU' : U' ≤ g ⁻¹ᵁ U)
    (Φ : (ModuleCat.extendScalars (g.appLE U U' hU').hom).obj
        (ModuleCat.of Γ(X, U) Γ(M, U)) ≅
      ModuleCat.of Γ(X', U') Γ((Scheme.Modules.pullback g).obj M, U'))
    (hΦ : ∀ b : Γ(M, U), Φ.hom ((1 : Γ(X', U')) ⊗ₜ[Γ(X, U), (g.appLE U U' hU').hom] b) =
      Scheme.Modules.pullbackSection g M U U' hU' b)
    (e : Γ(M, U) ≃ₗ[Γ(X, U)] Γ(X, U)) :
    ∃ e' : Γ((Scheme.Modules.pullback g).obj M, U') ≃ₗ[Γ(X', U')] Γ(X', U'),
      ∀ b : Γ(M, U),
        e' (Scheme.Modules.pullbackSection g M U U' hU' b) = g.appLE U U' hU' (e b) := by
  have hΦ' : ∀ b : Γ(M, U),
      Φ.toLinearEquiv ((1 : Γ(X', U')) ⊗ₜ[Γ(X, U), (g.appLE U U' hU').hom] b) =
        Scheme.Modules.pullbackSection g M U U' hU' b :=
    fun b => (Iso.toLinearEquiv_apply Φ _).trans (hΦ b)
  have hb : Function.Bijective (fun t : Γ(X', U') =>
      t ⊗ₜ[Γ(X, U), (g.appLE U U' hU').hom] e.symm 1) :=
    @bijective_tmul_symm_one Γ(X, U) Γ(X', U') Γ(M, U) _ _
      (Module.compHom _ (g.appLE U U' hU').hom) _ _ e
  set m₀ : Γ((Scheme.Modules.pullback g).obj M, U') :=
    Scheme.Modules.pullbackSection g M U U' hU' (e.symm 1) with hm₀
  -- Stated and proved in term mode throughout: `Φ` applied to a pure tensor is type-correct
  -- only at default transparency, so a goal mentioning it is not available to `rw`.
  have hsmul : ∀ t : Γ(X', U'),
      t • m₀ = Φ.toLinearEquiv (t ⊗ₜ[Γ(X, U), (g.appLE U U' hU').hom] e.symm 1) := fun t =>
    (congrArg (fun z : Γ((Scheme.Modules.pullback g).obj M, U') => t • z)
        (hm₀.trans (hΦ' (e.symm 1)).symm)).trans
      ((Φ.toLinearEquiv.map_smul t
          ((1 : Γ(X', U')) ⊗ₜ[Γ(X, U), (g.appLE U U' hU').hom] e.symm 1)).symm.trans
        (congrArg Φ.toLinearEquiv
          ((ModuleCat.ExtendScalars.smul_tmul (g.appLE U U' hU').hom t 1 (e.symm 1)).trans
            (congrArg (fun s : Γ(X', U') =>
              s ⊗ₜ[Γ(X, U), (g.appLE U U' hU').hom] e.symm 1) (mul_one t)))))
  have hbij : Function.Bijective (fun t : Γ(X', U') => t • m₀) := by
    have hcomp : (fun t : Γ(X', U') => t • m₀) =
        Φ.toLinearEquiv ∘ (fun t : Γ(X', U') =>
          t ⊗ₜ[Γ(X, U), (g.appLE U U' hU').hom] e.symm 1) := funext hsmul
    rw [hcomp]
    exact Φ.toLinearEquiv.bijective.comp hb
  refine ⟨(LinearEquiv.ofBijective
    (LinearMap.toSpanSingleton Γ(X', U') Γ((Scheme.Modules.pullback g).obj M, U') m₀)
      hbij).symm, fun b => ?_⟩
  refine (LinearEquiv.symm_apply_eq _).mpr ?_
  show Scheme.Modules.pullbackSection g M U U' hU' b = g.appLE U U' hU' (e b) • m₀
  exact ((hΦ' b).symm.trans (congrArg Φ.toLinearEquiv
      (@tmul_one_eq_tmul_symm_one Γ(X, U) Γ(X', U') Γ(M, U) _ _
        (Module.compHom _ (g.appLE U U' hU').hom) _ _ (g.appLE U U' hU').hom (fun _ _ => rfl)
        e b))).trans (hsmul (g.appLE U U' hU' (e b))).symm

/-- **A trivialization of a quasi-coherent module on an affine open pulls back** to a
trivialization on an affine open of the source mapping into it, and under it the local equation of
the pullback of a section is the image of its local equation. -/
theorem exists_linearEquiv_pullbackSection {X' : Scheme.{u}} (g : X' ⟶ X) (M : X.Modules)
    [M.IsQuasicoherent] {U : X.Opens} (hU : IsAffineOpen U) {U' : X'.Opens}
    (hU'a : IsAffineOpen U') (hU' : U' ≤ g ⁻¹ᵁ U) (e : Γ(M, U) ≃ₗ[Γ(X, U)] Γ(X, U)) :
    ∃ e' : Γ((Scheme.Modules.pullback g).obj M, U') ≃ₗ[Γ(X', U')] Γ(X', U'),
      ∀ b : Γ(M, U),
        e' (Scheme.Modules.pullbackSection g M U U' hU' b) = g.appLE U U' hU' (e b) :=
  exists_linearEquiv_pullbackSection_of_iso g M hU'
    (affinePullbackSectionsBaseChangeIso g M hU hU'a hU')
    (affinePullbackSectionsBaseChangeIso_one_tmul g M hU hU'a hU') e

/-- The restriction to `U'` of the pullback of a global section is the pullback of its
restriction to `U`. -/
theorem map_pullbackGlobalSections {X' : Scheme.{u}} (g : X' ⟶ X) (M : X.Modules)
    {U : X.Opens} {U' : X'.Opens} (hU' : U' ≤ g ⁻¹ᵁ U) (a : Γ(M, ⊤)) :
    ((Scheme.Modules.pullback g).obj M).presheaf.map (homOfLE (le_top : U' ≤ ⊤)).op
        (pullbackGlobalSections g M a) =
      Scheme.Modules.pullbackSection g M U U' hU'
        (M.presheaf.map (homOfLE (le_top : U ≤ ⊤)).op a) := by
  have htop : (⊤ : X'.Opens) ≤ g ⁻¹ᵁ (⊤ : X.Opens) := by simp
  have hU'top : U' ≤ g ⁻¹ᵁ (⊤ : X.Opens) := by simp
  rw [pullbackGlobalSections_eq_pullbackSection g M htop a,
    pullbackSection_res_target g M (le_top : U' ≤ ⊤) htop hU'top a,
    pullbackSection_res_source g M (le_top : U ≤ ⊤) hU'top hU' a]

/-- **The local equation of the pullback of a global section is the image of its local
equation.** -/
theorem exists_linearEquiv_pullbackGlobalSections {X' : Scheme.{u}} (g : X' ⟶ X) (M : X.Modules)
    [M.IsQuasicoherent] {U : X.Opens} (hU : IsAffineOpen U) {U' : X'.Opens}
    (hU'a : IsAffineOpen U') (hU' : U' ≤ g ⁻¹ᵁ U) (e : Γ(M, U) ≃ₗ[Γ(X, U)] Γ(X, U))
    (a : Γ(M, ⊤)) :
    ∃ e' : Γ((Scheme.Modules.pullback g).obj M, U') ≃ₗ[Γ(X', U')] Γ(X', U'),
      e' (((Scheme.Modules.pullback g).obj M).presheaf.map (homOfLE (le_top : U' ≤ ⊤)).op
          (pullbackGlobalSections g M a)) =
        g.appLE U U' hU' (e (M.presheaf.map (homOfLE (le_top : U ≤ ⊤)).op a)) := by
  obtain ⟨e', he'⟩ := exists_linearEquiv_pullbackSection g M hU hU'a hU' e
  refine ⟨e', ?_⟩
  rw [map_pullbackGlobalSections g M hU' a]
  exact he' _

/-- **The ideal of the zero scheme of a pulled-back global section on an affine open of the
source** is generated by the image of the local equation. -/
theorem zeroScheme_ideal_pullbackGlobalSections {X' : Scheme.{u}} (g : X' ⟶ X) (M : X.Modules)
    [AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsInvertible X.sheaf.obj X.ringCatSheaf.property M]
    (U : X.affineOpens) (U' : X'.affineOpens) (hU' : U'.1 ≤ g ⁻¹ᵁ U.1)
    (e : Γ(M, U.1) ≃ₗ[Γ(X, U.1)] Γ(X, U.1)) (a : Γ(M, ⊤)) :
    (zeroScheme X' ((Scheme.Modules.pullback g).obj M)
        (pullbackGlobalSections g M a)).ideal U' =
      Ideal.span ({g.appLE U.1 U'.1 hU'
        (e (M.presheaf.map (homOfLE (le_top : U.1 ≤ ⊤)).op a))} : Set Γ(X', U'.1)) := by
  have : M.IsQuasicoherent := isQuasicoherent_of_isInvertible M
  obtain ⟨e', he'⟩ := exists_linearEquiv_pullbackGlobalSections g M U.2 U'.2 hU' e a
  exact zeroScheme_ideal_of_trivialization X' ((Scheme.Modules.pullback g).obj M)
    (pullbackGlobalSections g M a) U' e' _ he'

end Stacks.Divisors

